        {
          "published_at": "2026-11-09T00:16:46.490Z",
          "url": "https://x.com/HamelHusain/status/2119584949032693767",
          "topic": "Why teams need private task-specific evals instead of public benchmark picking",
          "text": "I see some are drawing the wrong inference from this study: they are focusing on this meta benchmark as yet another benchmark for model picking, i.e. open vs closed models, model families etc.  \n\nThat’s too narrow of an interpretation!  You need to do your own private evals on your specific tasks to know what’s “better”\n\nThis should give you healthy skepticism of all public benchmarks.  I believe that was the intention of this illustration to begin with.",
          "attachments": [],
          "quote_tweet": {
            "url": "https://x.com/loresjpg/status/2118880329490637049",
            "published_at": "2026-11-07T01:36:52.100Z",
            "author": {
              "name": "Justin Lo",
              "handle": "loresjpg"
            },
            "text": "Nice DeepSWE score! Does it survive a lowercase filename?\n\nIntroducing MaxxBench: 89 DeepSWE tasks with small changes to the instructions or starting code. Same engineering problem, slightly different requirement.\n\nModels clustered around 74% on DeepSWE end up 23 pp apart.\n\nGood",
